From: Kokosa Flake
Subject: [PATCH] seccomp: classify process group creation with spawning

Venus starts a separate render server and gives it a process group.
Allow setpgid when process spawning is explicitly enabled, without allowing
UID/GID changes or disabling the remaining sandbox policy.

--- a/system/qemu-seccomp.c
+++ b/system/qemu-seccomp.c
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@ static const struct QemuSeccompSyscall denylist[] = {
       0, NULL, SCMP_ACT_TRAP },
     { SCMP_SYS(setgid),                 QEMU_SECCOMP_SET_PRIVILEGED,
       0, NULL, SCMP_ACT_TRAP },
-    { SCMP_SYS(setpgid),                QEMU_SECCOMP_SET_PRIVILEGED,
+    { SCMP_SYS(setpgid),                QEMU_SECCOMP_SET_SPAWN,
       0, NULL, SCMP_ACT_TRAP },
     { SCMP_SYS(setsid),                 QEMU_SECCOMP_SET_PRIVILEGED,
       0, NULL, SCMP_ACT_TRAP },
